<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My, central concern with this as a story is that you're setting up Dr Fox as the protagonist of the story but they aren't actually a particularly active part of the story, instead being dragged from event to event where she just kinda, reacts to what's happening in a pretty passive way instead of like, her actually being the driving force of the story.</p>
<p>Beyond this, it's just&#8230;not very interesting as a narrative? There's a murder monster, it does some murder, it disappears, there's a bit of investigation and then we learn <em>why</em> it does murders but there's not really any sense of there being like&#8230;stakes to this discovery or anything and it doesn't really reframe what's happening in an interesting way.</p>
<p>I guess really what this needs is character motivation: Fox needs a reason to be so invested in figuring out what's happening beyond just 'its her job!'; and the dark dog needs a reason to like&#8230;have this whole ritual happen and to attack the other dogs. I think the ritual also just kinda passively happening feels weird too? Like, nothing makes it happen and so it's just&#8230;kinda a thing that happens to happen. The angle of there being like, Damien and this dog working together to manifest the dark dog isn't awful but it needs to feel purposeful: like, if this was them manifesting a dark dog to like, get revenge on the people that wronged Damien or to hunt down his murderer or w/e, it'd land a lot better; but instead it's just&#8230;a weird ritual?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

