			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863649">
									

<p>Hello. I couldn’t be able to go into detail because of the word number restriction.<br />
Now with your concerns.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>1) Fox wanted to know why this dog is forming in the way of ritual, and because they can’t talk to a dog, they started to observe, and this is the big meat of the story for me. Fox is trying to understand why this ritual is happening.</p>
<hr />
<p>Its a bit of a spoiler but: I want Fox to be morally conflicted, one of the observation days, she ordered the dogs to be killed to see what will happen if the ritual cut short and stuff happens that it ended up having Her disciplinary leave. People around did not like what she did and hated her for it. But then when she learned about what the roommate did she’ll be so angry about that she dragged the roommate where this Dog was and had him get killed by it.</p>
<hr />
<p>2) The ritual is also one thing I’m still developing, but the dogs realised since almost all of them are stray know that this entity is a bit unstable for a dog, and even it can’t or won’t eat humans, but it will kill person, but when tested. The dog was Damian pet, and while dying, it had immense hatred towards human and other dogs (since a group of people killed them) them enough to form a whole entity. The reason this dog wasn’t hunting the killers down was because of these dogs. (But if this does not feel natural, I would just take it out entirely.)</p>
<p>3) The Roommate was in significant debt, and because Damian was a rich kid, the roommate begged for money, and he did get the money, but he never paid the debt back and blamed Damian for it which resulted in his death. All of this, is Fox interviewing the roommate and doing an investigation.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope this makes sense.</p>

